sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Reproducibility package: 85/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Re-running `--no-show --out --csv --gif` reproduced the committed PNG, CSV and GIF byte-for-byte (SHA-256 73edc6ae..., 2b6efe3a..., df4acc7a...), the pipeline uses no RNG so no seed is needed, requirements.lock.txt pins exact versions with Python 3.14.7 / macOS arm64 and the venv matches (numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, pillow 12.0.0), fixtures are SHA-pinned and the run fails closed on mismatch, and `--self-test` passes in about 1.5 s. -5: the README section documents only `--gif PATH`; `--self-test`, `--no-show`, `--out` and `--csv` appear only in argparse. -4: `from scipy.special import iv as bessel_iv` is unused (the script has its own power series), so scipy is a spurious hard dependency. -3: the default `--gif` path is the repo root while the committed asset lives in docs/media, so the documented invocation does not regenerate the shipped file in place. -3: the README claims parity <= 6.7e-16 while the run reports 2.22e-16, a stale number that should be generated, not hand-written. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1326–L1343: argparse flags --out/--csv/--gif/--no-show/--self-test; outputs byte-identical on re-run <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1326-L1343>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L5: exact pip freeze with Python 3.14.7, macOS arm64, 2026-10-17 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L5>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L69–L69: unused scipy import bessel_iv <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L69-L69>; README.md L484–L488: documents only --gif PATH and claims <= 6.7e-16 parity <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/README.md#L484-L488>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Reproducibility package' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

